In 2023, Fountain University and Al-Hikmah University, Ilorin, formalized a strategic academic partnership through a Memorandum of Understanding designed to promote collaboration in teaching, research, innovation, and institutional development.

The collaboration is founded on the shared vision of both institutions to strengthen academic excellence through the exchange of knowledge, expertise, and resources while advancing scholarship for national and global development.

The Memorandum of Understanding provides a comprehensive framework for collaboration in several key areas, including:
• Joint research projects and scholarly publications;
• Staff and student exchange programmes;
• Collaborative academic conferences, workshops, seminars, and training programmes;
• Exchange of academic publications and educational resources;
• Shared access to specialized laboratories, research facilities, and academic infrastructure; and
• Capacity-building initiatives aimed at strengthening institutional effectiveness.

This partnership enables both universities to leverage their respective strengths, broaden academic opportunities for staff and students, and promote multidisciplinary research capable of addressing contemporary societal challenges.

By encouraging collaboration rather than competition, the partnership fosters an academic environment where ideas, innovation, and expertise transcend institutional boundaries. It further enhances the quality of teaching and research while preparing graduates with the knowledge, skills, global perspective, and collaborative spirit required to succeed in an increasingly interconnected world.

The collaboration also reflects Fountain University's unwavering commitment to building enduring partnerships that enrich the educational experience, strengthen research productivity, and contribute meaningfully to sustainable national development.

In 2023, Fountain University entered into a strategic partnership with the Nigerian Air Force (NAF) through the signing of a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU), reaffirming the University's commitment to delivering education, research, and innovation that respond to national development priorities and emerging global challenges.

The collaboration brings together the academic expertise of Fountain University and the technical and strategic capabilities of the Nigerian Air Force to promote capacity building, scientific advancement, technology transfer, and professional development in areas of national importance.

The partnership provides opportunities for collaborative teaching, research, specialised professional training, and certification programmes in several interdisciplinary fields, including:
• Cybersecurity;
• Artificial Intelligence;
• Governance and Strategic Studies;
• Communication Strategy and Crisis Management;
• Software Development and Robotics;
• Procurement and Logistics Management; and
• Other emerging areas of science, technology, and national security.

The Memorandum of Understanding also promotes staff exchanges, collaborative research projects, joint conferences, seminars, workshops, and specialized short-term academic programmes, creating a vibrant platform for knowledge sharing and innovation between both institutions.

Through this partnership, Fountain University continues to strengthen its contribution to national capacity building by producing graduates equipped with the technical expertise, leadership skills, and strategic thinking required to address contemporary challenges in public service, industry, defence, and national development.

The collaboration further reinforces the University's commitment to fostering innovation, interdisciplinary research, and strategic partnerships that create lasting value for society.
